      {
        "finding": "Standard N=1 models with more layers (44M to 160M parameters) show perplexity falling 17.69, 10.27, 9.42, 8.42, 8.34, flattening at the top on 10M tokens. No power law is fitted.",
        "proposed_claim": "Data-bound parameter scaling saturates (descriptive only).",
